            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " is an annotation that can be applied to a test class to configure metadata that is used to determine how to load and configure an "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "ApplicationContext"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for integration tests. Specifically, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@ContextConfiguration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " declares the application context resource "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "locations"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " or the component "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "classes"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " used to load the context."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
        "inlines": [
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": "Resource locations are typically XML configuration files or Groovy scripts located in the classpath, while component classes are typically "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Configuration"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " classes. However, resource locations can also refer to files and scripts in the file system, and component classes can be "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Component"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " classes, "
          },
          {
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "@Service"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "monospace",
            "roles": []
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " classes, and so on. See "
          },
          {
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Component Classes"
              }
            ],
            "kind": "xref",
            "target": "testing/testcontext-framework/ctx-management/javaconfig.html#testcontext-ctx-management-javaconfig-component-classes"
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "value": " for further details."
          }
        ],
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "context": "paragraph",
        "id": null,
